-- An UNDECLARED chain of a user-defined operator under a built-in
-- connective stays an error now that user-infix operands are admitted
-- under built-ins: there is no default fixity, so the flat chain does not
-- re-associate and the operator is applied to 4 arguments (compare
-- not-ok/tc/fixity-undeclared-chain.l4, the same rule at top level).
GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
      y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
x PLAIN y MEANS x PLUS y

#EVAL 1 PLAIN 2 PLAIN 3 OR TRUE
